# stray local build of cmd/benchharness, anchored so it cannot also swallow new files under cmd/benchharness/
/benchharness

# stray local build of cmd/queuelabrun, anchored so it cannot also swallow new files under cmd/queuelabrun/
/queuelabrun

# Raw chaos-run records were excluded here, and queuelab inherited the rule without anyone asking whether it
# fit. It does not. This lab's thesis is that the record outlives the terminal and that a conclusion nobody
# can re-derive is prose -- and its records sat outside version control while committed documents told
# readers to run `queuelabrun -compare 'ex/e14-*.json'` against files that do not ship.
#
# It cost what you would expect. A pre-registration fixed the GPU session's baseline at a figure assembled at
# a shell from records that were then deleted, and the number appears in no record that exists. Git is the
# notary a pre-registration needs; declining it left half the evidence with an mtime and nothing else.
#
# So run records are committed and the rest of ex/ -- scratch output, ad-hoc blobs -- is not. The whole
# directory is 248 KB.
ex/*
!ex/*.json
